==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|fr|bataillon}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/bəˈtæliən/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-battalion.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|military}} An [[army]] [[unit]] having two or more [[company|companies]], etc. and a [[headquarters]]. Traditionally forming part of a [[regiment]].
# {{lb|en|US|military}} an army unit having two or more companies, etc. and a headquarters; forming part of a [[brigade]].
# Any large [[body]] of [[troops]].
# {{lb|en|by extension}} A [[great]] [[number]] of things.

====Synonyms====
